{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Tax all political donations on receipt at 50 percent",
        "additional_details": "If donations are taxed in this way, companies or individuals that want to promote their own interests or beliefs of whatever sort by supporting a political party will also be supporting the country as a whole by raising money in tax revenue. Consideration could also be given to this rule applying to non-currency donations to parties and MPs \u2013 for example, if an MP is given tickets to a football match the MP can either except the gift and pay 50% of the value of the ticket in tax or not accept the gift.",
        "background": "We want the Government to tax all political donations on receipt at 50%. The aim of this is to reduce political interference with elections while helping fund public services.",
